{"title":"Radical","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Radicals</b> are basically the opposite of exponents.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d3cd7247af9e3ff395331ee9ca4eeef60bafd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> can be denoted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae4bfb7aa330a9e563213cb40914e1b66e26383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radical&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">Algebra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Exponentiation\" title=\"Exponentiation\">Exponent</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Radical&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018104613\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 262/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 352/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.243      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.243      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9723:|#|:idhash:canonical an